module main

-- §11.4/§14.4 (POSITIVE) — carrier recovery through a primitive equand. The
-- IsProp-under-Pi closure solver discharges 'IsProp (forall xs. l = r)' only
-- when it can recover the equands' OWN carrier and that carrier is a set.
--
-- Here an equand is '__debugRender 1' (the rendering primitive), whose result
-- type is 'String'. The carrier-recovery walk ('equandType') must read 'String'
-- off a primitive equand and thread the prelude's 'instance IsSet String' into
-- 'isPropEq'. An earlier walk under-applied the primitive's declared Pi
-- telescope — dropping its erased implicit '@0 a : Type' parameter and returning
-- a stuck/partial codomain — so it falsely DECLINED this true String carrier
-- (a conservative false negative; soundness-safe but incomplete). With the
-- telescope walked correctly the obligation discharges.
--
-- The dual soundness guards stay closed: a FALSE 'Bool' equality (Bool is not a
-- set) is still REJECTED, and a foreign set-typed rigid merely occurring in a
-- stuck equand is still never grabbed as the carrier — see
-- isprop-eq-foreign-carrier-rigid-rejected.kp and
-- isprop-eq-requires-isset-bool-subst-rejected.kp.

descrLaw : (=) String (__debugRender 1) ""
let descrLaw = unsafeAssertProof "a String law over a primitive equand"

--! mode check
--! allow_unsafe_assert_proof
--! assertNoErrors
--! assertAuditLedger unsafeAssertProof
